---
/**
 * Blog index (`/blog`) — Phase D3. Built and SHIPPED DISABLED.
 *
 * See build-context/DECISIONS.md ("Blog is built and DELIBERATELY DISABLED") and
 * docs/enable-blog.md before touching anything in this file's behaviour.
 *
 * ⚠️ FILENAME DEVIATION FROM THE ORIGINAL BRIEF — READ BEFORE "FIXING" THIS.
 * The brief asked for `src/pages/blog/index.astro`. This file is named
 * `[...page].astro` instead, and that is deliberate, not a mistake to clean up.
 *
 * Empirically verified during this build (repeated, cache-cleared, from-scratch
 * trials — not a guess, and not merely "unlinked"): in this Astro version,
 * `getStaticPaths()` returning `[]` has NO EFFECT on a non-dynamic page file (one
 * with no `[param]` in its filename, e.g. a plain `index.astro`). Astro renders a
 * non-dynamic route unconditionally, because it has exactly one implicit path and
 * doesn't need enumeration — the exported `getStaticPaths` function is simply never
 * invoked. A plain `blog/index.astro` guarded by `if (!features.blog) return []`
 * was built and tested: `dist/blog/index.html` was emitted anyway, every time, flag
 * or no flag. That fails GATE 3 outright — an indexable, crawlable `/blog` page
 * shipping while `features.blog` is `false`, exactly the failure mode the brief
 * calls "worse than not having built the blog at all."
 *
 * `getStaticPaths()` DOES work reliably on genuinely dynamic (bracketed) routes —
 * confirmed both by this file and independently by `blog/[slug].astro` and the
 * case-study system's `project/[slug].astro`. So this file uses Astro's *rest*
 * parameter (`[...page]`) to become a dynamic route that can resolve to the exact
 * same URL, `/blog` (no trailing segment, matching `trailingSlash: 'never'`), while
 * actually letting `getStaticPaths()` govern whether it exists. An *optional single*
 * segment (`[[page]]`) was tried first and rejected: Astro's static-path validator
 * throws `GetStaticPathsExpectedParams` if `params` has no keys, and separately
 * throws `Missing parameter` if a required-looking dynamic segment's value is
 * `undefined` — there is no value that satisfies both checks for `[[page]]`. A rest
 * parameter has neither problem: its own resolver (`params[key] ?? ''`, in Astro's
 * route generator) treats an `undefined` value as "no segment" instead of throwing,
 * so `getStaticPaths()` returning `[{ params: { page: undefined } }]` legitimately
 * generates the bare `/blog` URL. The `page` param is never real — this file only
 * ever returns `[]` or that one entry — it exists purely so Astro classifies the
 * route as dynamic. Named `page` (not `slug`) specifically to avoid any ambiguity
 * with the sibling `[slug].astro` article route; despite both routes structurally
 * overlapping (a rest param matches any depth, including one segment), Astro's
 * route priority favours the more specific `[slug]` match for real article paths,
 * and this file's own `getStaticPaths()` never generates a one-segment path anyway
 * — confirmed empirically: both `/blog` and `/blog/example-post` build correctly
 * side by side with no route-collision error.
 *
 * GATE 3 of 6 (docs/enable-blog.md's six-gate checklist): route suppression.
 * `getStaticPaths()` returns `[]` whenever `features.blog` is false — the committed
 * value in src/config.ts — so Astro emits zero files under `dist/blog/` for the
 * index. Verified against the actual build output, not assumed.
 *
 * When enabled, this mirrors projects.astro's hero + card-grid shape exactly, and
 * reuses ProjectCard.astro rather than inventing a parallel BlogCard component — a
 * post summary (title/description/tags/image/href) is the same shape as a project
 * summary. ProjectCard is only imported here, never edited (D3 does not own it).
 *
 * Posts without a `heroImage` are filtered out of the grid: ProjectCard requires an
 * image, and `heroImage` is intentionally optional at the schema level (not every
 * post need have one) — so a post that omits it simply doesn't appear as a card
 * until it has one. docs/enable-blog.md calls this out for anyone adding real posts.
 */
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro'
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SectionShell from '../../components/SectionShell.astro'
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro'
import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro'
import { features } from '../../config'

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  if (!features.blog) return []
  return [{ params: { page: undefined } }]
}

const allPosts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft)

const posts = allPosts
  .filter((post): post is typeof post & { data: { heroImage: ImageMetadata } } =>
    Boolean(post.data.heroImage),
  )
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.publishDate.valueOf() - a.data.publishDate.valueOf())
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Blog | Leviathan Core"
  description="Insights, updates, and behind-the-scenes stories from the Leviathan Core team."
  canonicalPath="/blog"
>
  <SectionShell sectionClass="section-blog-hero" withTopDivider={false}>
    <div class="blog-hero-grid">
      <SectionHeading as="h1" variant="display-2xl" class="blog-hero-heading">
        News &amp; Insights
      </SectionHeading>
      <p class="lead-text">
        Updates, perspectives, and behind-the-scenes stories from the team connecting brands and
        audiences in the gaming space.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionShell>

  {
    posts.length > 0 && (
      <section class="section-blog-posts">
        <div class="page-padding">
          <div class="container-xxlarge">
            <div class="blog-posts-list">
              {posts.map((post) => (
                <div class="blog-posts-item">
                  <ProjectCard
                    title={post.data.title}
                    description={post.data.description}
                    tags={post.data.tags}
                    image={post.data.heroImage}
                    imageAlt={post.data.heroImageAlt ?? post.data.title}
                    href={`/blog/${post.id}`}
                    ctaText="Read Article"
                  />
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    max-width: var(--measure-lead);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .blog-hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    align-items: end;
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {
    .blog-hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .blog-hero-heading {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 10ch;
  }

  .blog-posts-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .blog-posts-item {
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 12%, transparent);
  }
  .blog-posts-item:first-child {
    border-top: none;
  }
</style>
